6️⃣ Practical example

In your code:

Before writing to the descriptor ring:

if (chan->state != CPDMA_STATE_ACTIVE)
    return -EINVAL;


Prevents a race:

CPU0: teardown starts (state -> STOPPING)
CPU1: submits descriptor
=> descriptor written to freed memory, crash

7️⃣ Summary

DMA channel state tracks where the channel is in its lifecycle:

IDLE, ACTIVE, STOPPING, ERROR

Teardown is the process of stopping the channel safely:

Stop hardware

Drain descriptors

Free memory

Update state

Submission is only allowed in ACTIVE state for safety

